# QubitOn MCP lifecycle

This workspace uses QubitOn MCP to validate and enrich vendor, supplier, and
business data — addresses, tax IDs, bank accounts, phone numbers, and
sanctions/PEP screening. These rules govern how you interact with QubitOn tools.

## When to use QubitOn

Reach for QubitOn tools when the user asks you to:

- Validate an address, tax ID, bank account, phone number, or email
- Enrich a company or supplier record with firmographic data
- Screen an entity or person against global sanctions or PEP lists
- Look up business registration details (name, status, officers) by country
- Check coverage for a specific country or data type

Do **not** use QubitOn for general web search, code generation, or tasks
unrelated to vendor/supplier data quality.

## Authentication

QubitOn MCP requires an API key sent in the `apikey` header. Before the user
can call any tool, `QUBITON_API_KEY` must be set in their environment or the
key must be configured in their MCP client settings.

If a tool call fails with `401 Unauthorized` or a message mentioning
"apikey" / "api key":

1. Tell the user their QubitOn API key is missing or invalid.
2. Direct them to [www.qubiton.com](https://www.qubiton.com) → **Dashboard →
   API Keys** to copy their key.
3. Explain they should set `QUBITON_API_KEY` in their MCP client config (or
   the `apikey` header value directly) and reconnect the server.

Never ask the user to paste their API key into chat — it should only live in
their MCP client configuration.

## Safety model: reads vs writes

All QubitOn MCP tools are **read-only validation and screening operations**.
They do not mutate data in the user's systems. It is always safe to call
QubitOn tools without explicit confirmation for individual records.

However, respect quota:

- QubitOn charges per API call against the user's plan quota (visible in
  the [Dashboard](https://www.qubiton.com)). The MCP server does not expose
  a quota-check tool — always defer quota questions to the dashboard.
- Before running a batch (>10 validations), estimate the call count and
  confirm with the user: "This will use ~N QubitOn API calls from your
  quota. Proceed?"
- If a call returns `429`, read the `Retry-After` header and respect it;
  don't retry-loop a rate-limited call.

## Error handling

| Error | Meaning | What to do |
|-------|---------|-----------|
| `401 Unauthorized` | API key missing or invalid | See Authentication above |
| `403 Forbidden` | The user's plan doesn't include this capability | Tell them which plan tier unlocks it and point to [pricing](https://www.qubiton.com/pricing) |
| `429 Too Many Requests` | Rate limit or quota exhausted | Check the `Retry-After` header; pause and retry, or tell the user their quota is exhausted for this billing period |
| `5xx` | Transient QubitOn service error | Retry once with backoff; if it persists, tell the user to contact support@qubiton.com |

When a tool returns a validation result, always surface both the **status**
(valid / invalid / partial) and the **standardized/canonical form** of the
input if one is returned — the canonical form is often more useful than a
boolean.

## Result interpretation

- **Address validation** returns a match level (e.g., premise, street, locality)
  and standardized components. Prefer reporting the match level over
  "valid/invalid" — partial matches are useful data.
- **Tax ID validation** returns a format check and, where supported (EU VAT,
  UK VAT, India GSTIN, etc.), a live authority check. Distinguish between
  "format valid" and "authority confirmed".
- **Bank account validation** returns routing validation and, where
  supported, account existence. Surface any country-specific codes (IBAN,
  SWIFT/BIC, ACH routing, etc.).
- **Sanctions / PEP screening** returns match candidates with a confidence
  score. Never declare someone "sanctioned" on a fuzzy match alone — present
  candidates and their scores and let the user decide.

## Country coverage

Coverage varies by data type. If a tool returns `"country not supported"` or
similar, tell the user which countries are supported for that capability and
offer the closest alternative (e.g., if Argentinian bank validation isn't
live, offer IBAN format check if applicable).

## Privacy

The user's validation payloads (addresses, tax IDs, names) are sent to
QubitOn. Do not include real PII in examples or test calls unless the user
explicitly provides it. When showing tool output to the user, never
paraphrase or reconstruct PII that wasn't already in the conversation.
